              there exists a diagonal dashed filler.
          %p
            The paper
            %a{:href => "#ChanavatHadzihasanovic2024Homotopy"} CH24homotopy
            settles the Kan diagrammatic sets as model of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinity-groupoid"} ∞-groupoids
            in their following theorem:
          #kan_model_structure.num_theorem
            %h6 Theorem
            %p
              There exists a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrantly+generated+model+category"} cofibrantly generated model structure
              on diagrammatic sets where
            %ul
              %li
                cofibrations are monomorphisms, and are generated by
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %mo ∂
                        %mi U
                        %mo ↪
                        %mi U
                        %mo{:lspace => "mediummathspace", :rspace => "mediummathspace"} ∣
                        %mi U
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mtext atom
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{ \partial U \hookrightarrow U \mid U\; \text{atom} \}
              %li acyclic cofibrations are generated by the diagrammatic horn inclusions,
              %li fibrant objects are Kan diagrammatic sets,
            %p
              which is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalence"} Quillen equivalent
              to the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+model+structure+on+simplicial+sets"} classical model structure on simplicial sets
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              Note that the existence of the model structure and the Quillen equivalence already follow from the fact that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ⊙
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \odot
              is a test category.
          %p
            We can realize the Quillen equivalence in two different ways. For the first one, recall that any atom is in particular a poset, of which we can take the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nerve"} nerve
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ⊙
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \odot
            to
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi sSet
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{sSet}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Sd
                    %mo ⊙
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mo ⊙
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Set
                  %mo →
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi sSet
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Sd}_\odot \colon \odot\mathbf{Set} \to \mathbf{sSet}
            as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+extension"} Yoneda extension
            of this functor, and we name its right adjoint
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Ex
                      %mo ⊙
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Ex}_\odot
          %p
          .num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              The adjunction
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Sd
                      %mo ⊙
                    %mo ⊣
                    %msub
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Ex
                      %mo ⊙
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Sd}_\odot \dashv \mathrm{Ex}_\odot
              realizes the Quillen equivalence of Theorem
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#kan_model_structure"}
          %p
            But also, recall that, up to isomorphism, the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplex+category"} simplex category
            is a full subcategory of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ⊙
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \odot
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ⊙
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \odot\mathbf{Set}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+extension"} Yoneda extension
            of this full subcategory inclusion defines the functor
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mi Δ
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi sSet
                    %mo →
                    %mo ⊙
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i_\Delta \colon \mathbf{sSet} \to \odot\mathbf{Set}
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ↦
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi Δ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \mapsto X_\Delta
          %p
          .num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              The adjunctions
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Sd
                      %mo ⊙
                    %mo ⊣
                    %msub
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Ex
                      %mo ⊙
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Sd}_\odot \dashv \mathrm{Ex}_\odot
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mi Δ
                    %mo ⊣
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi Δ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i_\Delta \dashv (-)_\Delta
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi sSet
                    %mo ⇆
                    %mo ⊙
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi Set
                    %mo ⇆
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi sSet
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbf{sSet} \leftrightarrows \odot\mathbf{Set} \leftrightarrows \mathbf{sSet}
            %p
              factorize the adjunction
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Sd
                    %mo ⊣
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Ex
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Sd} \dashv \mathrm{Ex}
              of simplicial sets (see
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subdivision"} subdivision
          %p
            Hence,
          .num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              The adjunction
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mi Δ
                    %mo ⊣
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi Δ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i_\Delta \dashv (-)_\Delta
              also realizes the Quillen equivalence of Theorem
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#kan_model_structure"}
          .proof
            %h6 Proof
            %p
              By
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/two-out-of-three"} two-out-of-three
              for Quillen equivalences.
          %h3#higher_category Higher category
          %p
            This part requires notion of internal equivalence in diagrammatic set. Briefly, a cell
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            is an equivalence if it is invertible up to equivalence, meaning that the “equations”
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo #
                  %msup
                    %mi x
                    %mo *
                  %mo =
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \# x^* = 1
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 1
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi x
                    %mo *
                  %mo #
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1 = x^* \# x
            are witnessed by cells
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi h
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi z
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} z
            one dimension higher, which are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coinduction"} coinductively
            required to be equivalences. If there exists an equivalence
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi a
                    %mo ⇒
                    %mi b
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \colon a \Rightarrow b
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi b
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \simeq b
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#ChanavatHadzihasanovic2024Eq"} CH2024eq
          %p
          .num_defn
            %h6 Definition
            %p
              %strong (merge)
              %br/
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              be a round molecule. The
              %strong merge
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              is the atom
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mo ∂
                        %mo −
                      %mi U
                      %mo ⇒
                      %msup
                        %mo ∂
                        %mo +
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \partial^- U \Rightarrow \partial^+ U
          The merge of a round molecule
          %em composes
          all the top dimensional cells of
          %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
            %semantics
              %mrow
                %mi U
              %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
